# Repo-root ignores. Backend/frontend have their own, narrower
# `.gitignore` files (`backend/.gitignore`, `frontend/.gitignore`) for their
# package-specific build/cache artefacts; this one covers root-level and
# cross-cutting concerns (CLAUDE.md: "No secrets in the repo" — added as
# part of P6-T01 since this compose stack introduces a root-level `.env`).

# Never commit a real environment file — only the checked-in `*.env.example`
# templates are tracked.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!backend/.env.example
!frontend/.env.example

.DS_Store

# Local overrides some operators may create alongside docker-compose.yml
# (e.g. `docker-compose.override.yml` for a per-host TLS cert mount path) —
# not part of this task's scope to define, but ignored by default so one
# doesn't get committed by accident.
docker-compose.override.yml

# DEV-ONLY self-signed TLS material generated by
# `deploy/tls/generate-dev-cert.sh` (P6-T02) — a throwaway cert/key pair for
# local `make dev` only, regenerated on demand, never the production
# artifact (see that script's own header comment). The generator script
# itself IS tracked; its output is not.
deploy/tls/dev/

# Docker Compose secrets material (P6-T04) — real secret files an operator
# generates/populates under secrets/ (or deploy/secrets/generate-dev-
# secrets.sh auto-generates for local dev only — throwaway values, never the
# production artifact). Only this directory's own README and .gitkeep are
# tracked; every other file under secrets/ is ignored, including any future
# secret added there (e.g. a P6-T03 oidc_client_secret.txt).
secrets/*
!secrets/.gitkeep
!secrets/README.md
